-- PART 9 -- Enforcement (regulations 75 to 92 of the Money Laundering, Terrorist Financing and
-- Transfer of Funds (Information on the Payer) Regulations 2017, S.I. 2017/692, United Kingdom),
-- lines 2448-2755 of uksi-2017-692.txt.
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively.  The text is a plain-text rendering made by a converter
-- script; it is not the official text, and nothing here is verified against the official text.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER.  A decision function answers JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING.
-- JUST FALSE is the text saying no in its own words; each such branch carries
-- `-- FALSE-kind (...)` with the quoted words.  NOTHING is "the text does not answer"; each such
-- branch carries `-- NOTHING-kind (...)`.  A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Marginal readings, listed in NOTES.md: (a) a failed "applies if", a trailing "if" on a power,
-- an "is"-definition and a flat negative are the text's no; (b) a grant or a prohibition limited
-- by its own wording is not a no; (c) a "must" that has not been done is the text's no.
-- Rulings of 2026-11-05, tagged `[ruled 2026-11-05 (a) period]` and `[ruled 2026-11-05 (b) where]`
-- on the branch (they are not the marginal readings above): a period the text fixes in its own
-- words answers JUST FALSE outside it; a "where" condition that is not met answers JUST FALSE;
-- a scope limit with no "only" answers NOTHING outside the scope.
-- A duty function (a "must") answers JUST FALSE only for a breach.  Where the duty arises "if" or
-- "where" something holds, a companion function, `... the duty ... arises`, answers JUST FALSE when
-- it does not arise, and the duty function answers NOTHING then.
-- A seam is marked `-- SEAM S-n (asking|answering)`.

§ `Part 9 -- Enforcement`

§§ `Chapter 1 -- General`

§§ `Regulation 75 -- Meaning of relevant requirement`

-- Reg 75: "relevant requirement" has the meaning given in Schedule 6.  Schedule 6 belongs to part mlr5; its answer is an input.
-- src:2451 | For the purposes of this Part, “relevant requirement” has the meaning given in Schedule 6.
@ref reg 75 (src:2451)
-- SEAM S-17 (asking)
GIVEN `sch 6 the provision is a relevant requirement` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 75 the requirement is a relevant requirement` IS
    CONSIDER `sch 6 the provision is a relevant requirement`
    WHEN JUST listed THEN
        IF listed
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“relevant requirement” has the meaning given in Schedule 6" [marginal (a)]
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): Schedule 6 has not answered

§§ `Chapter 2 -- Civil penalties and notices`

§§ `Regulation 76 -- Power to impose civil penalties: fines and statements`

-- Reg 76(8)(b): "designated supervisory authority" means the FCA or the Commissioners.
-- src:2467 | (8) For the purposes of this regulation—
-- src:2468 | (a) “appropriate” means (other than in references to an appropriate body) effective, proportionate and dissuasive;
-- src:2469 | (b) “designated supervisory authority” means the FCA or the Commissioners.
@ref reg 76(8) (src:2467-2469)
@ref reg 76(8)(b) (src:2469)
GIVEN body IS AN Authority
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 76(8)(b) the body is a designated supervisory authority` IS
    IF     body EQUALS `the Financial Conduct Authority`
        OR body EQUALS `the Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“designated supervisory authority” means the FCA or the Commissioners"

-- Reg 76(8)(a): "appropriate" means effective, proportionate and dissuasive, except in references to an appropriate body (where the paragraph gives no meaning).
@ref reg 76(8)(a) (src:2468)
GIVEN `the word is used in a reference to an appropriate body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is effective` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is proportionate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is dissuasive` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 76(8)(a) the penalty or measure is appropriate` IS
    IF `the word is used in a reference to an appropriate body`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the paragraph defines "appropriate" "other than in references to an appropriate body", and gives no meaning there
    ELSE IF `it is effective` AND `it is proportionate` AND `it is dissuasive`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“appropriate” means ... effective, proportionate and dissuasive"

-- Reg 76(1): paragraph (2) applies if a designated supervisory authority is satisfied that P has contravened a relevant requirement imposed on P.
-- src:2454 | (1) Paragraph (2) applies if a designated supervisory authority is satisfied that any person (“P”) has contravened a relevant requirement imposed on that person.
@ref reg 76(1) (src:2454)
GIVEN `reg 76(8)(b) the body is a designated supervisory authority` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the authority is satisfied that P has contravened a requirement imposed on P` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reg 75 the requirement is a relevant requirement` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 76(1) paragraph (2) applies` IS
    IF (`reg 76(8)(b) the body is a designated supervisory authority` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND `the authority is satisfied that P has contravened a requirement imposed on P` AND (`reg 75 the requirement is a relevant requirement` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF (NOT (`reg 76(8)(b) the body is a designated supervisory authority` EQUALS JUST FALSE)) AND `the authority is satisfied that P has contravened a requirement imposed on P` AND (NOT (`reg 75 the requirement is a relevant requirement` EQUALS JUST FALSE))
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): an answer that another provision gives is not in
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Paragraph (2) applies if a designated supervisory authority is satisfied that any person (“P”) has contravened a relevant requirement imposed on that person" [marginal (a)]

-- Reg 76(2): what a designated supervisory authority may do when paragraph (2) applies: one or both.
-- src:2455 | (2) A designated supervisory authority may do one or both of the following—
-- src:2456 | (a) impose a penalty of such amount as it considers appropriate on P;
-- src:2457 | (b) publish a statement censuring P.
@ref reg 76(2) (src:2455-2457)
DECLARE `reg 76(2) measure` IS ONE OF
    `reg 76(2)(a) impose a penalty of such amount as it considers appropriate on P`
    `reg 76(2)(b) publish a statement censuring P`
    `reg 76(2) some other measure`

@ref reg 76(2) (src:2455-2457)
GIVEN `reg 76(1) paragraph (2) applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      what IS A `reg 76(2) measure`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 76(2) the designated supervisory authority may` IS
    IF `reg 76(1) paragraph (2) applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN CONSIDER what
         WHEN `reg 76(2)(a) impose a penalty of such amount as it considers appropriate on P` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `reg 76(2)(b) publish a statement censuring P` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `reg 76(2) some other measure` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the items are listed and the text does not say others are barred
    ELSE IF `reg 76(1) paragraph (2) applies` EQUALS JUST FALSE
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Paragraph (2) applies if a designated supervisory authority is satisfied that any person (“P”) has contravened a relevant requirement imposed on that person" [marginal (a)]
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): reg 76(1) paragraph (2) applies has not been answered

-- Reg 76(3): the penalty on an officer who was knowingly concerned.  The officer's status is a core term (S-K4), answered as at the material time.  "If" is the whole condition (marginal reading (a)): an officer who was not knowingly concerned, or a person who is not an officer, answers JUST FALSE; the answer is NOTHING only where an answer that another provision gives is not in.
-- src:2458 | (3) If a designated supervisory authority considers that another person who was at the material time an officer of P was knowingly concerned in a contravention of a relevant requirement by P, the designated supervisory authority may impose on that person a penalty of such amount as it considers appropriate.
@ref reg 76(3) (src:2458)
-- SEAM S-K4 (asking)
GIVEN `reg 76(8)(b) the body is a designated supervisory authority` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `reg 3(1) the person is an officer of the entity` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the authority considers that the officer was knowingly concerned in a contravention of a relevant requirement by P` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reg 75 the requirement is a relevant requirement` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 76(3) the designated supervisory authority may impose a penalty on the officer` IS
    IF (`reg 76(8)(b) the body is a designated supervisory authority` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`reg 3(1) the person is an officer of the entity` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND `the authority considers that the officer was knowingly concerned in a contravention of a relevant requirement by P` AND (`reg 75 the requirement is a relevant requirement` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF (NOT (`reg 76(8)(b) the body is a designated supervisory authority` EQUALS JUST FALSE)) AND (NOT (`reg 3(1) the person is an officer of the entity` EQUALS JUST FALSE)) AND `the authority considers that the officer was knowingly concerned in a contravention of a relevant requirement by P` AND (NOT (`reg 75 the requirement is a relevant requirement` EQUALS JUST FALSE))
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): an answer that another provision gives is not in
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a designated supervisory authority considers that another person who was at the material time an officer of P was knowingly concerned in a contravention of a relevant requirement by P" [marginal (a)]

-- Reg 76(4): a flat negative with the bearer named (the authority).  JUST FALSE: it may not impose a penalty on P.  The penalty on an officer under paragraph (3) is outside it.
-- src:2459 | (4) A designated supervisory authority must not impose a penalty on P under this regulation for contravention of a relevant requirement if the authority is satisfied that P took all reasonable steps and exercised all due diligence to ensure that the requirement would be complied with.
@ref reg 76(4) (src:2459)
GIVEN `the penalty is imposed on P under this regulation for contravention of a relevant requirement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authority is satisfied that P took all reasonable steps and exercised all due diligence to ensure that the requirement would be complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 76(4) the designated supervisory authority may impose a penalty on P` IS
    IF `the penalty is imposed on P under this regulation for contravention of a relevant requirement` AND `the authority is satisfied that P took all reasonable steps and exercised all due diligence to ensure that the requirement would be complied with`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A designated supervisory authority must not impose a penalty on P under this regulation for contravention of a relevant requirement" [marginal (a)]
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the authority is satisfied that P took all reasonable steps and exercised all due diligence"

-- Reg 76(4), the prohibition on the authority (the bearer the text names), derived from the answer above (ruling N2).
DECLARE `reg 76(4) party` IS ONE OF
    `reg 76(4) the designated supervisory authority`

DECLARE `reg 76(4) action` IS ONE OF
    `reg 76(4) the designated supervisory authority imposes a penalty on P`

@ref reg 76(4) (src:2459)
GIVEN `reg 76(4) the designated supervisory authority may impose a penalty on P` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `reg 76(4) party` `reg 76(4) action`
DECIDE `reg 76(4) the prohibition on the designated supervisory authority` IS
    IF `reg 76(4) the designated supervisory authority may impose a penalty on P` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN PARTY `reg 76(4) the designated supervisory authority`
         SHANT `reg 76(4) the designated supervisory authority imposes a penalty on P`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `reg 76(4) the designated supervisory authority` BECAUSE "the designated supervisory authority imposed a penalty on P although it was satisfied that P took all reasonable steps and exercised all due diligence, which regulation 76(4) forbids"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- Reg 76(5): the FCA consults the PRA before imposing a penalty on a PRA-authorised person or a person with a qualifying relationship with one.
-- src:2460 | (5) Where the FCA proposes to impose a penalty under this regulation on a PRA-authorised person or on a person who has a qualifying relationship with a PRA-authorised person, it must consult the PRA.
@ref reg 76(5) (src:2460)
GIVEN `the FCA proposes to impose a penalty under this regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a PRA-authorised person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has a qualifying relationship with a PRA-authorised person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 76(5) the duty to consult the PRA arises` IS
    IF `the FCA proposes to impose a penalty under this regulation` AND (`the person is a PRA-authorised person` OR `the person has a qualifying relationship with a PRA-authorised person`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the FCA proposes to impose a penalty under this regulation on a PRA-authorised person or on a person who has a qualifying relationship with a PRA-authorised person" [ruled 2026-11-05 (b) where]
@ref reg 76(5) (src:2460)
GIVEN `the FCA proposes to impose a penalty under this regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a PRA-authorised person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has a qualifying relationship with a PRA-authorised person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the FCA consulted the PRA` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 76(5) the FCA consulted the PRA` IS
    IF `the FCA proposes to impose a penalty under this regulation` AND (`the person is a PRA-authorised person` OR `the person has a qualifying relationship with a PRA-authorised person`)
    THEN IF `the FCA consulted the PRA`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it must consult the PRA" [marginal (c)]
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where the FCA proposes to impose a penalty under this regulation on a PRA-authorised person or on a person who has a qualifying relationship with a PRA-authorised person"; the duty does not arise, so there is no answer here: ask `reg 76(5) the duty to consult the PRA arises`

-- Reg 76(6): guidance the authority must consider when deciding whether P has contravened.  Limb (a) is blank in this text (line 2462).
-- Which guidance counts: (b)(i) guidance issued by the FCA; (b)(ii) guidance issued by another supervisory authority or appropriate body and approved by the Treasury.
-- src:2461 | (6) In deciding whether P has contravened a relevant requirement, the designated supervisory authority must consider whether at the time P followed—
-- src:2462 | (a) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:2463 | (b) any relevant guidance which was at the time—
-- src:2464 | (i) issued by the FCA; or
-- src:2465 | (ii) issued by any other supervisory authority or appropriate body and approved by the Treasury.
@ref reg 76(6) (src:2461-2465)
GIVEN `the guidance was at the time issued by the FCA` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the guidance was at the time issued by another supervisory authority or an appropriate body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the guidance was approved by the Treasury` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 76(6)(b) the guidance is guidance the authority must consider` IS
    IF `the guidance was at the time issued by the FCA` OR (`the guidance was at the time issued by another supervisory authority or an appropriate body` AND `the guidance was approved by the Treasury`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any relevant guidance which was at the time— (i) issued by the FCA; or (ii) issued by any other supervisory authority or appropriate body and approved by the Treasury" [marginal (a)]

GIVEN `the authority is deciding whether P has contravened a relevant requirement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reg 76(6)(b) the guidance is guidance the authority must consider` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the authority considered whether at the time P followed the guidance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 76(6) the authority considered whether P followed the guidance` IS
    IF `the authority is deciding whether P has contravened a relevant requirement` AND (`reg 76(6)(b) the guidance is guidance the authority must consider` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN IF `the authority considered whether at the time P followed the guidance`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the designated supervisory authority must consider whether at the time P followed" [marginal (c)]
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In deciding whether P has contravened a relevant requirement"

-- Reg 76(7): who a penalty is payable to.
-- src:2466 | (7) A penalty imposed under this Part is payable to the designated supervisory authority which imposes it.
@ref reg 76(7) (src:2466)
GIVEN `the penalty is imposed under this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body that imposes it` IS AN Authority
GIVETH A MAYBE Authority
DECIDE `reg 76(7) the penalty is payable to` IS
    IF `the penalty is imposed under this Part` AND `reg 76(8)(b) the body is a designated supervisory authority` `the body that imposes it` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST `the body that imposes it`
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A penalty imposed under this Part is payable to the designated supervisory authority which imposes it"

§§ `Regulation 77 -- Power to impose civil penalties: suspension and removal of authorisation`

-- Reg 77(1): paragraph (2) applies if the FCA is satisfied that a relevant person or a payment service provider has done one of five things.
-- src:2471 | (1) Paragraph (2) applies if the FCA is satisfied that a relevant person or a payment service provider has—
-- src:2472 | (a) repeatedly or systematically failed to include the information it is required to include on the payer or the payee under Articles 4, 5 or 6 of the funds transfer regulation;
-- src:2473 | (b) failed to implement effective risk-based procedures in breach of Articles 8 or 12 of the funds transfer regulation;
-- src:2474 | (c) failed to comply with Articles 11, 12 or 16 of the funds transfer regulation, where the failure is a serious one;
-- src:2475 | (d) repeatedly or systematically failed to retain records in breach of Article 16 of the funds transfer regulation; or
-- src:2476 | (e) failed to comply with a relevant requirement.
@ref reg 77(1) (src:2471-2476)
GIVEN `the FCA is satisfied of one of the following` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reg 8 the person is a relevant person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is a payment service provider` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has repeatedly or systematically failed to include the information it is required to include on the payer or the payee under Articles 4, 5 or 6 of the funds transfer regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has failed to implement effective risk-based procedures in breach of Articles 8 or 12 of the funds transfer regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has failed to comply with Articles 11, 12 or 16 of the funds transfer regulation and the failure is a serious one` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has repeatedly or systematically failed to retain records in breach of Article 16 of the funds transfer regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has failed to comply with a relevant requirement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 77(1) paragraph (2) applies` IS
    IF `the FCA is satisfied of one of the following` AND ((`reg 8 the person is a relevant person` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR `the person is a payment service provider`) AND (`the person has repeatedly or systematically failed to include the information it is required to include on the payer or the payee under Articles 4, 5 or 6 of the funds transfer regulation` OR `the person has failed to implement effective risk-based procedures in breach of Articles 8 or 12 of the funds transfer regulation` OR `the person has failed to comply with Articles 11, 12 or 16 of the funds transfer regulation and the failure is a serious one` OR `the person has repeatedly or systematically failed to retain records in breach of Article 16 of the funds transfer regulation` OR `the person has failed to comply with a relevant requirement`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `the FCA is satisfied of one of the following` AND ((NOT (`reg 8 the person is a relevant person` EQUALS JUST FALSE)) OR `the person is a payment service provider`) AND (`the person has repeatedly or systematically failed to include the information it is required to include on the payer or the payee under Articles 4, 5 or 6 of the funds transfer regulation` OR `the person has failed to implement effective risk-based procedures in breach of Articles 8 or 12 of the funds transfer regulation` OR `the person has failed to comply with Articles 11, 12 or 16 of the funds transfer regulation and the failure is a serious one` OR `the person has repeatedly or systematically failed to retain records in breach of Article 16 of the funds transfer regulation` OR `the person has failed to comply with a relevant requirement`)
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): an answer that another provision gives is not in
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Paragraph (2) applies if the FCA is satisfied that a relevant person or a payment service provider has—" [marginal (a)]

-- Reg 77(2): the measures the FCA may take: (a) cancel or suspend one of five permissions, authorisations or registrations; (b) impose limitations or restrictions of five kinds.  "One or more" of them.
-- src:2477 | (2) The FCA may take one or more of the measures set out in sub-paragraphs (a) and (b)—
-- src:2478 | (a) to cancel or suspend, for such period as it considers appropriate—
-- src:2479 | (i) any permission which an authorised person has to carry on a regulated activity;
-- src:2480 | (ii) the authorisation of a payment service provider as an authorised payment institution under the Payment Services Regulations 2017;
-- src:2481 | (iii) the registration of a payment service provider as a small payment institution under the Payment Services Regulations 2017;
-- src:2482 | (iv) the authorisation of a payment service provider as an authorised electronic money institution under the Electronic Money Regulations 2011 ; or
-- src:2483 | (v) the registration of a payment service provider as a small electronic money institution under the Electronic Money Regulations 2011;
-- src:2484 | (b) to impose, for such period as it considers appropriate, such limitations or other restrictions as it considers appropriate—
-- src:2485 | (i) in relation to the carrying on of a regulated activity by an authorised person;
-- src:2486 | (ii) on the authorisation of a payment service provider as a payment institution under the Payment Services Regulations 2017;
-- src:2487 | (iii) on the registration of a payment service provider as a small payment institution under the Payment Services Regulations 2017;
-- src:2488 | (iv) on the authorisation of a payment service provider as an electronic money institution under the Electronic Money Regulations 2011; or
-- src:2489 | (v) on the registration of a payment service provider as a small electronic money institution under the Electronic Money Regulations 2011.
@ref reg 77(2) (src:2477-2489)
DECLARE `reg 77(2) measure` IS ONE OF
    `reg 77(2)(a)(i) cancel or suspend any permission which an authorised person has to carry on a regulated activity`
    `reg 77(2)(a)(ii) cancel or suspend the authorisation of a payment service provider as an authorised payment institution`
    `reg 77(2)(a)(iii) cancel or suspend the registration of a payment service provider as a small payment institution`
    `reg 77(2)(a)(iv) cancel or suspend the authorisation of a payment service provider as an authorised electronic money institution`
    `reg 77(2)(a)(v) cancel or suspend the registration of a payment service provider as a small electronic money institution`
    `reg 77(2)(b)(i) impose limitations or other restrictions in relation to the carrying on of a regulated activity by an authorised person`
    `reg 77(2)(b)(ii) impose limitations or other restrictions on the authorisation of a payment service provider as a payment institution`
    `reg 77(2)(b)(iii) impose limitations or other restrictions on the registration of a payment service provider as a small payment institution`
    `reg 77(2)(b)(iv) impose limitations or other restrictions on the authorisation of a payment service provider as an electronic money institution`
    `reg 77(2)(b)(v) impose limitations or other restrictions on the registration of a payment service provider as a small electronic money institution`
    `reg 77(2) some other measure`

@ref reg 77(2) (src:2477-2489)
GIVEN `reg 77(1) paragraph (2) applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      what IS A `reg 77(2) measure`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 77(2) the FCA may take the measure` IS
    IF `reg 77(1) paragraph (2) applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN CONSIDER what
         WHEN `reg 77(2)(a)(i) cancel or suspend any permission which an authorised person has to carry on a regulated activity` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `reg 77(2)(a)(ii) cancel or suspend the authorisation of a payment service provider as an authorised payment institution` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `reg 77(2)(a)(iii) cancel or suspend the registration of a payment service provider as a small payment institution` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `reg 77(2)(a)(iv) cancel or suspend the authorisation of a payment service provider as an authorised electronic money institution` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `reg 77(2)(a)(v) cancel or suspend the registration of a payment service provider as a small electronic money institution` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `reg 77(2)(b)(i) impose limitations or other restrictions in relation to the carrying on of a regulated activity by an authorised person` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `reg 77(2)(b)(ii) impose limitations or other restrictions on the authorisation of a payment service provider as a payment institution` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `reg 77(2)(b)(iii) impose limitations or other restrictions on the registration of a payment service provider as a small payment institution` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `reg 77(2)(b)(iv) impose limitations or other restrictions on the authorisation of a payment service provider as an electronic money institution` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `reg 77(2)(b)(v) impose limitations or other restrictions on the registration of a payment service provider as a small electronic money institution` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `reg 77(2) some other measure` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the items are listed and the text does not say others are barred
    ELSE IF `reg 77(1) paragraph (2) applies` EQUALS JUST FALSE
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Paragraph (2) applies if the FCA is satisfied that a relevant person or a payment service provider has—" [marginal (a)]
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): reg 77(1) paragraph (2) applies has not been answered

-- Reg 77(3): "permission" (a "means" definition) and "regulated activity" (a pointer to section 22 of FSMA, which is outside the sources).
