§§ `Regulation 78 -- Power to impose civil penalties: prohibitions on management`

-- Reg 78(1): paragraph (2) applies if a designated supervisory authority considers that another person who was at the material time an officer of P was knowingly concerned in a contravention by P.
-- src:2501 | (1) Paragraph (2) applies if a designated supervisory authority considers that another person who was at the material time an officer of P was knowingly concerned in a contravention of a relevant requirement by P.
@ref reg 78(1) (src:2501)
-- SEAM S-K4 (asking)
GIVEN `reg 76(8)(b) the body is a designated supervisory authority` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `reg 3(1) the person is an officer of the entity` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the authority considers that the officer was knowingly concerned in a contravention of a relevant requirement by P` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 78(1) paragraph (2) applies` IS
    IF (`reg 76(8)(b) the body is a designated supervisory authority` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`reg 3(1) the person is an officer of the entity` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND `the authority considers that the officer was knowingly concerned in a contravention of a relevant requirement by P`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF (NOT (`reg 76(8)(b) the body is a designated supervisory authority` EQUALS JUST FALSE)) AND (NOT (`reg 3(1) the person is an officer of the entity` EQUALS JUST FALSE)) AND `the authority considers that the officer was knowingly concerned in a contravention of a relevant requirement by P`
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): an answer that another provision gives is not in
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Paragraph (2) applies if a designated supervisory authority considers that another person who was at the material time an officer of P was knowingly concerned in a contravention of a relevant requirement by P" [marginal (a)]

-- Reg 78(2): the measures: a temporary or a permanent prohibition on having a management role.
-- src:2502 | (2) The designated supervisory authority may impose one of the following measures on the person concerned—
-- src:2503 | (a) a temporary prohibition on the individual concerned holding an office or position involving responsibility for taking decisions about the management of a relevant person or a payment service provider (“having a management role”);
-- src:2504 | (b) a permanent prohibition on the individual concerned having a management role.
