DECLARE `reg 78(2) measure` IS ONE OF
    `reg 78(2)(a) a temporary prohibition on the individual concerned having a management role`
    `reg 78(2)(b) a permanent prohibition on the individual concerned having a management role`
    `reg 78(2) some other measure`

@ref reg 78(2) (src:2502-2504)
GIVEN `reg 78(1) paragraph (2) applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      what IS A `reg 78(2) measure`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 78(2) the designated supervisory authority may impose the measure` IS
    IF `reg 78(1) paragraph (2) applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN CONSIDER what
         WHEN `reg 78(2)(a) a temporary prohibition on the individual concerned having a management role` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `reg 78(2)(b) a permanent prohibition on the individual concerned having a management role` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `reg 78(2) some other measure` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the items are listed and the text does not say others are barred
    ELSE IF `reg 78(1) paragraph (2) applies` EQUALS JUST FALSE
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Paragraph (2) applies if a designated supervisory authority considers that another person who was at the material time an officer of P was knowingly concerned in a contravention of a relevant requirement by P" [marginal (a)]
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): reg 78(1) paragraph (2) applies has not been answered

