§§ `Regulation 80 -- Injunctions`

-- Reg 80(1): on the application of a designated supervisory authority, the court may restrain (in Scotland, interdict) a contravention if satisfied of (a) or (b).
-- src:2514 | (1) If, on the application of a designated supervisory authority, the court is satisfied—
-- src:2515 | (a) that there is a reasonable likelihood that any person will contravene a relevant requirement; or
-- src:2516 | (b) that any person has contravened a relevant requirement and that there is a reasonable likelihood that the contravention will continue or be repeated,
-- src:2517 | the court may make an order restraining (or in Scotland an interdict prohibiting) the contravention.
@ref reg 80(1) (src:2514-2517)
GIVEN `the application is made by a designated supervisory authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that there is a reasonable likelihood that any person will contravene a relevant requirement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that any person has contravened a relevant requirement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that there is a reasonable likelihood that the contravention will continue or be repeated` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 80(1) the court may make an order restraining the contravention` IS
    IF `the application is made by a designated supervisory authority` AND (`the court is satisfied that there is a reasonable likelihood that any person will contravene a relevant requirement` OR (`the court is satisfied that any person has contravened a relevant requirement` AND `the court is satisfied that there is a reasonable likelihood that the contravention will continue or be repeated`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If, on the application of a designated supervisory authority, the court is satisfied— (a) that there is a reasonable likelihood that any person will contravene a relevant requirement; or (b) that any person has contravened a relevant requirement and that there is a reasonable likelihood that the contravention will continue or be repeated" [marginal (a)]

-- Reg 80(2): the court may order that person, and any other person who appears to have been knowingly concerned, to take steps to remedy the contravention.
-- src:2518 | (2) If on the application of a designated supervisory authority the court is satisfied—
-- src:2519 | (a) that any person has contravened a relevant requirement; and
-- src:2520 | (b) that there are steps which could be taken for remedying the contravention,
-- src:2521 | the court may make an order requiring that person, and any other person who appears to have been knowingly concerned in the contravention, to take such steps as the court may direct to remedy it.
