GIVEN `the application is made by a designated supervisory authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that any person has contravened a relevant requirement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that there are steps which could be taken for remedying the contravention` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 80(2) the court may make an order requiring the person to take steps to remedy the contravention` IS
    IF `the application is made by a designated supervisory authority` AND `the court is satisfied that any person has contravened a relevant requirement` AND `the court is satisfied that there are steps which could be taken for remedying the contravention`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If on the application of a designated supervisory authority the court is satisfied— (a) that any person has contravened a relevant requirement; and (b) that there are steps which could be taken for remedying the contravention" [marginal (a)]

-- Reg 80(3): the court may restrain a person who may have contravened, or been knowingly concerned, from dealing with assets it is satisfied that the person is reasonably likely to dispose of or deal with.
-- src:2522 | (3) If, on the application of a designated supervisory authority, the court is satisfied that any person may have—
-- src:2523 | (a) contravened a relevant requirement; or
-- src:2524 | (b) been knowingly concerned in the contravention of a relevant requirement,
-- src:2525 | the court may make an order restraining (or in Scotland an interdict prohibiting) that person from disposing or otherwise dealing with any assets belonging to that person which it is satisfied that that person is reasonably likely to dispose of or otherwise deal with.
@ref reg 80(3) (src:2522-2525)
GIVEN `the application is made by a designated supervisory authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that the person may have contravened a relevant requirement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that the person may have been knowingly concerned in the contravention of a relevant requirement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that the person is reasonably likely to dispose of or otherwise deal with assets belonging to that person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 80(3) the court may make an order restraining the person from disposing or otherwise dealing with the assets` IS
    IF `the application is made by a designated supervisory authority` AND (`the court is satisfied that the person may have contravened a relevant requirement` OR `the court is satisfied that the person may have been knowingly concerned in the contravention of a relevant requirement`) AND `the court is satisfied that the person is reasonably likely to dispose of or otherwise deal with assets belonging to that person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If, on the application of a designated supervisory authority, the court is satisfied that any person may have— (a) contravened a relevant requirement; or (b) been knowingly concerned in the contravention of a relevant requirement" [marginal (a)]

