§§ `Regulation 81 -- The FCA: disciplinary measures (procedure)`

-- Reg 81(1): what the FCA must take into account when determining the type of sanction and the level of any penalty.  "Including where appropriate" lists eight; "all relevant circumstances" reaches any other relevant one.
-- src:2529 | (1) When determining the type of sanction, and level of any penalty, to be imposed on a person (“P”) under regulation 76, 77 or 78, the FCA must take into account all relevant circumstances, including where appropriate—
-- src:2530 | (a) the gravity and the duration of the contravention or failure;
-- src:2531 | (b) the degree of responsibility of P;
-- src:2532 | (c) the financial strength of P;
-- src:2533 | (d) the amount of profits gained or losses avoided by P;
-- src:2534 | (e) the losses for third parties caused by the contravention or failure;
-- src:2535 | (f) the level of co-operation of P with the FCA;
-- src:2536 | (g) previous contraventions or failures by P; and
-- src:2537 | (h) any potential systemic consequences of the contravention or failure.
@ref reg 81(1) (src:2529-2537)
DECLARE `reg 81(1) circumstance` IS ONE OF
    `reg 81(1)(a) the gravity and the duration of the contravention or failure`
    `reg 81(1)(b) the degree of responsibility of P`
    `reg 81(1)(c) the financial strength of P`
    `reg 81(1)(d) the amount of profits gained or losses avoided by P`
    `reg 81(1)(e) the losses for third parties caused by the contravention or failure`
    `reg 81(1)(f) the level of co-operation of P with the FCA`
    `reg 81(1)(g) previous contraventions or failures by P`
    `reg 81(1)(h) any potential systemic consequences of the contravention or failure`
    `reg 81(1) some other circumstance`

@ref reg 81(1) (src:2529-2537)
GIVEN `the FCA is determining the type of sanction, or the level of any penalty, to be imposed on P under regulation 76, 77 or 78` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is appropriate to take the circumstance into account` IS A BOOLEAN
      what IS A `reg 81(1) circumstance`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 81(1) the FCA must take the circumstance into account` IS
    IF `the FCA is determining the type of sanction, or the level of any penalty, to be imposed on P under regulation 76, 77 or 78` AND `it is appropriate to take the circumstance into account`
    THEN CONSIDER what
         WHEN `reg 81(1)(a) the gravity and the duration of the contravention or failure` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `reg 81(1)(b) the degree of responsibility of P` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `reg 81(1)(c) the financial strength of P` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `reg 81(1)(d) the amount of profits gained or losses avoided by P` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `reg 81(1)(e) the losses for third parties caused by the contravention or failure` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `reg 81(1)(f) the level of co-operation of P with the FCA` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `reg 81(1)(g) previous contraventions or failures by P` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `reg 81(1)(h) any potential systemic consequences of the contravention or failure` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `reg 81(1) some other circumstance` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "When determining the type of sanction, and level of any penalty, to be imposed on a person (“P”) under regulation 76, 77 or 78, the FCA must take into account all relevant circumstances, including where appropriate—" [ruled 2026-11-05 (b) where (read from "when")]

