DECIDE `reg 81(3) the duty to consult the PRA arises` IS
    IF `the FCA proposes to impose a penalty` AND (`the person is a PRA-authorised person` OR `the person has a qualifying relationship with a PRA-authorised person`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the FCA proposes to impose a penalty on a PRA-authorised person or on a person who has a qualifying relationship with a PRA-authorised person" [ruled 2026-11-05 (b) where]
@ref reg 81(3) (src:2540)
GIVEN `the FCA proposes to impose a penalty` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a PRA-authorised person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has a qualifying relationship with a PRA-authorised person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the FCA consulted the PRA` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 81(3) the FCA consulted the PRA` IS
    IF `the FCA proposes to impose a penalty` AND (`the person is a PRA-authorised person` OR `the person has a qualifying relationship with a PRA-authorised person`)
    THEN IF `the FCA consulted the PRA`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it must consult the PRA" [marginal (c)]
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where the FCA proposes to impose a penalty on a PRA-authorised person or on a person who has a qualifying relationship with a PRA-authorised person"; the duty does not arise, so there is no answer here: ask `reg 81(3) the duty to consult the PRA arises`

-- Reg 81(4): section 387 of FSMA applies to the notice in paragraph (2) as to a warning notice under FSMA, subject to paragraph (5).  What section 387 says is outside the sources.
-- src:2541 | (4) Section 387 of FSMA (warning notices) applies in relation to a notice given under paragraph (2) as it applies in relation to a warning notice given by the FCA under that Act, subject to paragraph (5).
@ref reg 81(4) (src:2541)
