    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): what section 387 of FSMA says is not in the sources

-- Reg 81(5): what a warning notice must contain, according to what it is about.
-- src:2542 | (5) In complying with section 387(1)(a), a warning notice must—
-- src:2543 | (a) if it is about a proposal to publish a statement, set out the terms of the statement;
-- src:2544 | (b) if it is about a proposal to impose a penalty, specify the amount of the penalty;
-- src:2545 | (c) if it is about a proposal to impose a suspension, limitation or other restriction—
-- src:2546 | (i) state the period for which the suspension, limitation or restriction is to have effect,
-- src:2547 | (ii) sets out the terms of the suspension, limitation or other restriction;
-- src:2548 | (d) if it is about a proposal to cancel, state the date from which the cancellation is to have effect;
-- src:2549 | (e) if it is about a proposal to impose a prohibition on an individual, set out the terms of the proposed prohibition.
@ref reg 81(5) (src:2542-2549)
GIVEN `the warning notice is about a proposal to publish a statement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it sets out the terms of the statement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is about a proposal to impose a penalty` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it specifies the amount of the penalty` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is about a proposal to impose a suspension, limitation or other restriction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it states the period for which the suspension, limitation or restriction is to have effect` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it sets out the terms of the suspension, limitation or other restriction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is about a proposal to cancel` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it states the date from which the cancellation is to have effect` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is about a proposal to impose a prohibition on an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it sets out the terms of the proposed prohibition` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 81(5) the warning notice contains what it must` IS
    IF `the warning notice is about a proposal to publish a statement` OR `it is about a proposal to impose a penalty` OR `it is about a proposal to impose a suspension, limitation or other restriction` OR `it is about a proposal to cancel` OR `it is about a proposal to impose a prohibition on an individual`
    THEN IF ((NOT `the warning notice is about a proposal to publish a statement`) OR `it sets out the terms of the statement`) AND ((NOT `it is about a proposal to impose a penalty`) OR `it specifies the amount of the penalty`) AND ((NOT `it is about a proposal to impose a suspension, limitation or other restriction`) OR (`it states the period for which the suspension, limitation or restriction is to have effect` AND `it sets out the terms of the suspension, limitation or other restriction`)) AND ((NOT `it is about a proposal to cancel`) OR `it states the date from which the cancellation is to have effect`) AND ((NOT `it is about a proposal to impose a prohibition on an individual`) OR `it sets out the terms of the proposed prohibition`)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In complying with section 387(1)(a), a warning notice must— (a) if it is about a proposal to publish a statement, set out the terms of the statement" [marginal (c)]
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a warning notice about none of the five proposals is not governed by this paragraph

-- Reg 81(6): a decision to sanction needs a decision notice, without undue delay.  "Without undue delay" has no count of days in the text: whether it was met is a plain input.
