§§ `Regulation 83 -- The Commissioners: disciplinary measures (procedure)`

-- Reg 83(1): what the Commissioners must take into account.  Regulations 76 and 78 are named here, and 77 is not (it is the FCA's power).
-- src:2579 | (1) When determining the type of sanction, and level of any penalty, to be imposed on a person (“P”) under regulation 76 or 78, the Commissioners must take into account all relevant circumstances, including where appropriate—
-- src:2580 | (a) the gravity and the duration of the contravention or failure;
-- src:2581 | (b) the degree of responsibility of P;
-- src:2582 | (c) the financial strength of P;
-- src:2583 | (d) the amount of profits gained or losses avoided by P;
-- src:2584 | (e) the losses for third parties caused by the contravention or failure;
-- src:2585 | (f) the level of co-operation of P with the Commissioners;
-- src:2586 | (g) previous contraventions or failures by P; and
-- src:2587 | (h) any potential systemic consequences of the contravention or failure.
@ref reg 83(1) (src:2579-2587)
DECLARE `reg 83(1) circumstance` IS ONE OF
    `reg 83(1)(a) the gravity and the duration of the contravention or failure`
    `reg 83(1)(b) the degree of responsibility of P`
    `reg 83(1)(c) the financial strength of P`
    `reg 83(1)(d) the amount of profits gained or losses avoided by P`
    `reg 83(1)(e) the losses for third parties caused by the contravention or failure`
    `reg 83(1)(f) the level of co-operation of P with the Commissioners`
    `reg 83(1)(g) previous contraventions or failures by P`
    `reg 83(1)(h) any potential systemic consequences of the contravention or failure`
    `reg 83(1) some other circumstance`

@ref reg 83(1) (src:2579-2587)
GIVEN `the Commissioners are determining the type of sanction, or the level of any penalty, to be imposed on P under regulation 76 or 78` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is appropriate to take the circumstance into account` IS A BOOLEAN
      what IS A `reg 83(1) circumstance`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 83(1) the Commissioners must take the circumstance into account` IS
    IF `the Commissioners are determining the type of sanction, or the level of any penalty, to be imposed on P under regulation 76 or 78` AND `it is appropriate to take the circumstance into account`
    THEN CONSIDER what
         WHEN `reg 83(1)(a) the gravity and the duration of the contravention or failure` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `reg 83(1)(b) the degree of responsibility of P` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `reg 83(1)(c) the financial strength of P` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `reg 83(1)(d) the amount of profits gained or losses avoided by P` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `reg 83(1)(e) the losses for third parties caused by the contravention or failure` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `reg 83(1)(f) the level of co-operation of P with the Commissioners` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `reg 83(1)(g) previous contraventions or failures by P` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `reg 83(1)(h) any potential systemic consequences of the contravention or failure` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `reg 83(1) some other circumstance` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "When determining the type of sanction, and level of any penalty, to be imposed on a person (“P”) under regulation 76 or 78, the Commissioners must take into account all relevant circumstances, including where appropriate—" [ruled 2026-11-05 (b) where (read from "when")]

-- Reg 83(1A): the Commissioners check P's criminal convictions before imposing a sanction under 76, 77 or 78 (the text names regulation 77 here, which is the FCA's power).
