-- Reg 83(3): what the notice must give notice of.
-- src:2590 | (3) A notice must be given of—
-- src:2591 | (a) the Commissioners' decision—
-- src:2592 | (i) to impose a penalty, and the amount of the penalty;
-- src:2593 | (ii) to publish a statement, and the terms of the statement;
-- src:2594 | (iii) to impose a prohibition, and the terms of the prohibition;
-- src:2595 | (b) the Commissioners' reasons for imposing a penalty, publishing a statement or imposing a prohibition;
-- src:2596 | (c) the right to a review under regulation 94; and
-- src:2597 | (d) the right to appeal under regulation 99.
@ref reg 83(3) (src:2590-2597)
GIVEN `the notice is one the Commissioners must give under paragraph (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision is to impose a penalty` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice gives notice of the decision to impose a penalty and of the amount of the penalty` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision is to publish a statement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice gives notice of the decision to publish a statement and of the terms of the statement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision is to impose a prohibition` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice gives notice of the decision to impose a prohibition and of the terms of the prohibition` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice gives the Commissioners' reasons for imposing a penalty, publishing a statement or imposing a prohibition` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice gives notice of the right to a review under regulation 94` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice gives notice of the right to appeal under regulation 99` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 83(3) the notice contains what it must` IS
    IF `the notice is one the Commissioners must give under paragraph (2)`
    THEN IF ((NOT `the decision is to impose a penalty`) OR `the notice gives notice of the decision to impose a penalty and of the amount of the penalty`) AND ((NOT `the decision is to publish a statement`) OR `the notice gives notice of the decision to publish a statement and of the terms of the statement`) AND ((NOT `the decision is to impose a prohibition`) OR `the notice gives notice of the decision to impose a prohibition and of the terms of the prohibition`) AND `the notice gives the Commissioners' reasons for imposing a penalty, publishing a statement or imposing a prohibition` AND `the notice gives notice of the right to a review under regulation 94` AND `the notice gives notice of the right to appeal under regulation 99`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A notice must be given of— (a) the Commissioners' decision ...; (b) the Commissioners' reasons ...; (c) the right to a review under regulation 94; and (d) the right to appeal under regulation 99" [marginal (c)]
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in accordance with paragraph (3)"

-- Reg 83(4): a notice about a penalty must state how and by when it is to be paid, and how it may be recovered.
-- src:2598 | (4) A notice about a penalty must—
-- src:2599 | (a) state the manner in which and the period within which, the penalty is to be paid;
-- src:2600 | (b) give details of the way in which the penalty may be recovered if it is not paid by the date stated in the notice.
@ref reg 83(4) (src:2598-2600)
GIVEN `the notice is a notice about a penalty` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it states the manner in which and the period within which the penalty is to be paid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it gives details of the way in which the penalty may be recovered if it is not paid by the date stated in the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 83(4) the notice about a penalty contains what it must` IS
    IF `the notice is a notice about a penalty`
    THEN IF `it states the manner in which and the period within which the penalty is to be paid` AND `it gives details of the way in which the penalty may be recovered if it is not paid by the date stated in the notice`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A notice about a penalty must— (a) state the manner in which and the period within which, the penalty is to be paid; (b) give details of the way in which the penalty may be recovered" [marginal (c)]
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A notice about a penalty"

§§ `Regulation 84 -- Publication: the FCA`

-- Reg 84(1): a flat negative with two bearers named: the FCA, and any person to whom the warning notice is given or copied.  JUST FALSE: neither may publish the notice or any details.  Each bearer's prohibition is derived below (ruling N2).
-- src:2602 | (1) Where a warning notice is given by the FCA under regulation 81(2), neither the FCA nor any person to whom it is given or copied may publish the notice or any details concerning it.
@ref reg 84(1) (src:2602)
GIVEN `the notice is a warning notice given by the FCA under regulation 81(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 84(1) the FCA or a person to whom the warning notice is given or copied may publish it or any details concerning it` IS
    IF `the notice is a warning notice given by the FCA under regulation 81(2)`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "neither the FCA nor any person to whom it is given or copied may publish the notice or any details concerning it" [marginal (a)]
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a warning notice is given by the FCA under regulation 81(2)"

DECLARE `reg 84(1) FCA party` IS ONE OF
    `reg 84(1) the FCA`

DECLARE `reg 84(1) FCA action` IS ONE OF
    `reg 84(1) the FCA publishes the warning notice or details of it`

@ref reg 84(1) (src:2602)
GIVEN `reg 84(1) the FCA or a person to whom the warning notice is given or copied may publish it or any details concerning it` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `reg 84(1) FCA party` `reg 84(1) FCA action`
DECIDE `reg 84(1) FCA the prohibition on the FCA` IS
    IF `reg 84(1) the FCA or a person to whom the warning notice is given or copied may publish it or any details concerning it` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN PARTY `reg 84(1) the FCA`
         SHANT `reg 84(1) the FCA publishes the warning notice or details of it`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `reg 84(1) the FCA` BECAUSE "the FCA published a warning notice, or details of it, which regulation 84(1) forbids it to publish"
    ELSE FULFILLED

DECLARE `reg 84(1) recipient party` IS ONE OF
    `reg 84(1) a person to whom the notice is given or copied`

DECLARE `reg 84(1) recipient action` IS ONE OF
    `reg 84(1) the person publishes the warning notice or details of it`

@ref reg 84(1) (src:2602)
GIVEN `reg 84(1) the FCA or a person to whom the warning notice is given or copied may publish it or any details concerning it` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `reg 84(1) recipient party` `reg 84(1) recipient action`
DECIDE `reg 84(1) recipient the prohibition on a person to whom the notice is given or copied` IS
    IF `reg 84(1) the FCA or a person to whom the warning notice is given or copied may publish it or any details concerning it` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN PARTY `reg 84(1) a person to whom the notice is given or copied`
         SHANT `reg 84(1) the person publishes the warning notice or details of it`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `reg 84(1) a person to whom the notice is given or copied` BECAUSE "a person to whom a warning notice was given or copied published it, or details of it, which regulation 84(1) forbids"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- Reg 84(2): the FCA must publish such information as it considers appropriate about the matter of a decision notice, subject to paragraphs (3) to (9) (which can displace the duty).
