-- Reg 84(5): when the information must be published under paragraph (6) instead: if publishing the identity of a legal person or an individual's personal data would be disproportionate, or publishing would jeopardise financial-market stability or an ongoing investigation.  Subject to (8) and (9).
-- src:2606 | (5) Subject to paragraph (8) and (9), information about a matter to which a final notice relates must be published in accordance with paragraph (6) where—
-- src:2607 | (a) the FCA considers it to be disproportionate to publish the identity of a legal person on whom the sanction or measure is imposed following an assessment by the FCA of the proportionality of publishing the person's identity;
-- src:2608 | (b) the FCA considers it to be disproportionate to publish the personal data of the individual on whom the sanction or measure is imposed following an assessment by the FCA of the proportionality of publishing the personal data; or
-- src:2609 | (c) the publication of information under paragraph (4) would jeopardise the stability of the financial markets or an ongoing investigation.
@ref reg 84(5) (src:2606-2609)
GIVEN `the FCA considers it disproportionate to publish the identity of a legal person on whom the sanction or measure is imposed, following an assessment of the proportionality` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the FCA considers it disproportionate to publish the personal data of the individual on whom the sanction or measure is imposed, following an assessment of the proportionality` IS A BOOLEAN
      `publication of information under paragraph (4) would jeopardise the stability of the financial markets or an ongoing investigation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (8) or (9) displaces paragraph (5) in this case` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 84(5) the information must be published in accordance with paragraph (6)` IS
    IF (`the FCA considers it disproportionate to publish the identity of a legal person on whom the sanction or measure is imposed, following an assessment of the proportionality` OR `the FCA considers it disproportionate to publish the personal data of the individual on whom the sanction or measure is imposed, following an assessment of the proportionality` OR `publication of information under paragraph (4) would jeopardise the stability of the financial markets or an ongoing investigation`) AND (NOT `paragraph (8) or (9) displaces paragraph (5) in this case`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to paragraph (8) and (9), information about a matter to which a final notice relates must be published in accordance with paragraph (6) where—" [ruled 2026-11-05 (b) where]

-- Reg 84(6): where paragraph (5) applies the FCA must either defer publication until it ceases to apply, or publish on an anonymous basis if that would ensure the effective protection of the anonymised personal data.
-- src:2610 | (6) Where paragraph (5) applies, the FCA must—
-- src:2611 | (a) defer the publication of the information about a matter to which a final notice relates until such time as paragraph (5) ceases to apply; or
