    ELSE IF (NOT (`reg 84(5) the information must be published in accordance with paragraph (6)` EQUALS JUST FALSE))
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): an answer that another provision gives is not in
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where paragraph (5) applies, the FCA must— (a) defer the publication ...; or (b) publish the information on an anonymous basis" [ruled 2026-11-05 (b) where]
@ref reg 84(6) (src:2610-2612)
GIVEN `reg 84(5) the information must be published in accordance with paragraph (6)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the FCA deferred the publication until such time as paragraph (5) ceases to apply` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the FCA published the information on an anonymous basis` IS A BOOLEAN
      `publication on that basis would ensure the effective protection of any anonymised personal data in the information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
