      `the years the information remained on the official website` IS A NUMBER
      `the information is personal data` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the data protection legislation requires the information to be retained for a different period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information remained on the website for that different period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 84(10) the information remained on the website for long enough` IS
    IF `the FCA published information in accordance with paragraphs (2) to (8)`
    THEN IF `the years the information remained on the official website` >= 5 OR (`the information is personal data` AND `the data protection legislation requires the information to be retained for a different period` AND `the information remained on the website for that different period`)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the FCA must ensure that the information remains on its official website for at least five years, unless the information is personal data and the data protection legislation requires the information to be retained for a different period" [marginal (c)]
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where the FCA publishes information in accordance with paragraphs (2) to (8)"; the duty does not arise, so there is no answer here: ask `reg 84(10) the duty to keep the information on the website arises`

-- Reg 84(11): "personal data" is given its meaning by the Data Protection Act 2018; a pointer.
