-- Reg 85(4): as 84(5), for the Commissioners; subject to (7) and (8).
-- src:2626 | (4) Subject to paragraph (7) and (8), information about a matter to which a notice under regulation 83 relates must be published in accordance with paragraph (5) where—
-- src:2627 | (a) the Commissioners consider it to be disproportionate to publish the identity of a legal person on whom the sanction or measure is imposed following an assessment by the Commissioners of the proportionality of publishing the person's identity;
-- src:2628 | (b) the Commissioners consider it to be disproportionate to publish the personal data of the individual on whom the sanction or measure is imposed following an assessment by the Commissioners of the proportionality of publishing the personal data; or
-- src:2629 | (c) the publication of information under paragraph (3) would jeopardise the stability of the financial markets or an ongoing investigation.
@ref reg 85(4) (src:2626-2629)
GIVEN `the Commissioners consider it disproportionate to publish the identity of a legal person on whom the sanction or measure is imposed, following an assessment of the proportionality` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commissioners consider it disproportionate to publish the personal data of the individual on whom the sanction or measure is imposed, following an assessment of the proportionality` IS A BOOLEAN
      `publication of information under paragraph (3) would jeopardise the stability of the financial markets or an ongoing investigation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (7) or (8) displaces paragraph (4) in this case` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 85(4) the information must be published in accordance with paragraph (5)` IS
    IF (`the Commissioners consider it disproportionate to publish the identity of a legal person on whom the sanction or measure is imposed, following an assessment of the proportionality` OR `the Commissioners consider it disproportionate to publish the personal data of the individual on whom the sanction or measure is imposed, following an assessment of the proportionality` OR `publication of information under paragraph (3) would jeopardise the stability of the financial markets or an ongoing investigation`) AND (NOT `paragraph (7) or (8) displaces paragraph (4) in this case`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to paragraph (7) and (8), information about a matter to which a notice under regulation 83 relates must be published in accordance with paragraph (5) where—" [ruled 2026-11-05 (b) where]

-- Reg 85(5): as 84(6).
