§§ `Chapter 3 -- Criminal offences, penalties and proceedings etc.`

-- The two ways a person is convicted of an offence in this Chapter.  The penalty limits below are tested against them.
DECLARE `reg 86(1) mode of conviction` IS ONE OF
    `reg 86(1) on summary conviction`
    `reg 86(1) on conviction on indictment`

§§ `Regulation 86 -- Criminal offence`

-- Reg 86(1): a person who contravenes a relevant requirement imposed on that person is guilty of an offence.
-- src:2644 | (1) A person who contravenes a relevant requirement imposed on that person is guilty of an offence and liable—
-- src:2645 | (a) on summary conviction—
-- src:2646 | (i) in England and Wales, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding three months, to a fine or to both;
-- src:2647 | (ii) in Scotland or Northern Ireland, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding three months, to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum or to both;
-- src:2648 | (b) on conviction on indictment, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding two years, to a fine, or to both.
@ref reg 86(1) (src:2644-2648)
GIVEN `the person contravenes a requirement imposed on that person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reg 75 the requirement is a relevant requirement` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 86(1) the person is guilty of an offence` IS
    IF `the person contravenes a requirement imposed on that person` AND (`reg 75 the requirement is a relevant requirement` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person who contravenes a relevant requirement imposed on that person"

@ref reg 86(1) (src:2644-2648)
GIVEN `how the person is convicted` IS A `reg 86(1) mode of conviction`
      `the term of imprisonment, in months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 86(1) the term of imprisonment is within the liability` IS
    CONSIDER `how the person is convicted`
    WHEN `reg 86(1) on summary conviction` THEN
        IF `the term of imprisonment, in months` <= 3
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a)(i) in England and Wales, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding three months, to a fine or to both; (ii) in Scotland or Northern Ireland, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding three months" [marginal (a)]
    WHEN `reg 86(1) on conviction on indictment` THEN
        IF `the term of imprisonment, in months` <= 24
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) on conviction on indictment, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding two years, to a fine, or to both" [marginal (a)]
@ref reg 86(1) (src:2644-2648)
GIVEN `how the person is convicted` IS A `reg 86(1) mode of conviction`
      `where the person is convicted` IS A `Part of the United Kingdom`
      `the fine, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `the statutory maximum, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 86(1) the fine is within the liability` IS
    CONSIDER `how the person is convicted`
    WHEN `reg 86(1) on summary conviction` THEN
        IF `where the person is convicted` EQUALS `England and Wales`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "(i) in England and Wales, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding three months, to a fine or to both" states no figure
        ELSE IF `the fine, in pounds` <= `the statutory maximum, in pounds`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(ii) in Scotland or Northern Ireland, ... to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum or to both" [marginal (a)]
    WHEN `reg 86(1) on conviction on indictment` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "a fine" on conviction on indictment states no figure

-- Reg 86(2): in deciding whether a person has committed the offence, the court must decide whether the person followed any relevant guidance.  Limb (a) is blank in this text (line 2650).
-- src:2649 | (2) In deciding whether a person has committed an offence under paragraph (1), the court must decide whether that person followed—
-- src:2650 | (a) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:2651 | (b) any relevant guidance which was at the time—
-- src:2652 | (i) issued by the FCA; or
-- src:2653 | (ii) issued by any other supervisory authority or appropriate body and approved by the Treasury.
@ref reg 86(2) (src:2649-2653)
GIVEN `the guidance was at the time issued by the FCA` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the guidance was at the time issued by another supervisory authority or an appropriate body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the guidance was approved by the Treasury` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 86(2)(b) the guidance is guidance the court must consider` IS
    IF `the guidance was at the time issued by the FCA` OR (`the guidance was at the time issued by another supervisory authority or an appropriate body` AND `the guidance was approved by the Treasury`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any relevant guidance which was at the time— (i) issued by the FCA; or (ii) issued by any other supervisory authority or appropriate body and approved by the Treasury" [marginal (a)]

GIVEN `the court is deciding whether a person has committed an offence under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reg 86(2)(b) the guidance is guidance the court must consider` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the court decided whether the person followed the guidance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 86(2) the court decided whether the person followed the guidance` IS
    IF `the court is deciding whether a person has committed an offence under paragraph (1)` AND (`reg 86(2)(b) the guidance is guidance the court must consider` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN IF `the court decided whether the person followed the guidance`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the court must decide whether that person followed" [marginal (c)]
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In deciding whether a person has committed an offence under paragraph (1)"

-- Reg 86(3): a flat negative: not guilty if the person took all reasonable steps and exercised all due diligence.
-- src:2654 | (3) A person is not guilty of an offence under this regulation if that person took all reasonable steps and exercised all due diligence to avoid committing the offence.
@ref reg 86(3) (src:2654)
GIVEN `the person took all reasonable steps and exercised all due diligence to avoid committing the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 86(3) the person is guilty of an offence under this regulation` IS
    IF `the person took all reasonable steps and exercised all due diligence to avoid committing the offence`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person is not guilty of an offence under this regulation if that person took all reasonable steps and exercised all due diligence to avoid committing the offence" [marginal (a)]
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph says when a person is not guilty and nothing of when one is

-- Reg 86(1) and (3) gathered by hand (ruling E1, option B): is the person guilty of the offence under regulation 86?  Paragraph (3) is read first, because it is a flat negative.
