    IF `reg 86(3) the person is guilty of an offence under this regulation` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person is not guilty of an offence under this regulation if that person took all reasonable steps and exercised all due diligence" [marginal (a)]
    ELSE `reg 86(1) the person is guilty of an offence`

-- Reg 86(4): a person convicted of the offence is not also liable to a Chapter 2 sanction.
