    IF `the conduct constitutes an offence in any part of the United Kingdom` OR `the conduct would constitute an offence in any part of the United Kingdom if it occurred there`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Criminal conduct is conduct which— (a) constitutes an offence in any part of the United Kingdom; or (b) would constitute an offence in any part of the United Kingdom if it occurred there" [marginal (a)]

-- src:2671 | (5) A person benefits from conduct if that person obtains property as a result of or in connection with the conduct.
