    IF `the disclosure is to a client of the professional legal adviser, or to a representative of a client, in connection with the giving by the adviser of legal advice to the client` OR `the disclosure is to any person in connection with legal proceedings or contemplated legal proceedings`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a disclosure falls within this paragraph if it is a disclosure— (a) to (or to a representative of) a client of the professional legal adviser ...; or (b) to any person in connection with legal proceedings or contemplated legal proceedings" [marginal (a)]

