-- Reg 87(3): P does not commit an offence under paragraph (2)(a) if one of six cases holds.  A flat negative: JUST FALSE for each.  Each case is a separate fact; the Act-specific cases take a plain "made in the exercise of a function, or in compliance with a requirement" fact because the Acts are outside the sources.
-- src:2661 | (3) P does not commit an offence under paragraph (2)(a) if—
-- src:2662 | (a) P does not know or suspect that the disclosure is likely to prejudice the investigation;
-- src:2663 | (b) the disclosure is made in the exercise of a function under these Regulations, or in compliance with a requirement imposed by or under these Regulations;
-- src:2664 | (c) the disclosure is made in the exercise of a function, or in compliance with a requirement imposed, by or under the Terrorism Act 2000 ;
-- src:2665 | (d) the disclosure is made in the exercise of a function, or in compliance with a requirement imposed, by or under the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002 ;
-- src:2666 | (e) the disclosure is made in the exercise of a function, or in compliance with a requirement imposed, under any Act relating to criminal conduct or benefit from criminal conduct; or
-- src:2667 | (f) P is a professional legal adviser and the disclosure falls within paragraph (6).
@ref reg 87(3) (src:2661-2667)
DECLARE `reg 87(3) case` IS ONE OF
    `reg 87(3)(a) P does not know or suspect that the disclosure is likely to prejudice the investigation`
    `reg 87(3)(b) the disclosure is made in the exercise of a function under these Regulations, or in compliance with a requirement imposed by or under these Regulations`
    `reg 87(3)(c) the disclosure is made in the exercise of a function, or in compliance with a requirement imposed, by or under the Terrorism Act 2000`
    `reg 87(3)(d) the disclosure is made in the exercise of a function, or in compliance with a requirement imposed, by or under the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002`
    `reg 87(3)(e) the disclosure is made in the exercise of a function, or in compliance with a requirement imposed, under any Act relating to criminal conduct or benefit from criminal conduct`
    `reg 87(3)(f) P is a professional legal adviser and the disclosure falls within paragraph (6)`
    `reg 87(3) none of these cases`

@ref reg 87(3) (src:2661-2667)
GIVEN case IS A `reg 87(3) case`
      `reg 87(6) the disclosure falls within this paragraph` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `reg 87(7) the disclosure falls within paragraph (6)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 87(3) P commits an offence under paragraph (2)(a)` IS
    CONSIDER case
    WHEN `reg 87(3)(a) P does not know or suspect that the disclosure is likely to prejudice the investigation` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "P does not commit an offence under paragraph (2)(a) if— (a) P does not know or suspect that the disclosure is likely to prejudice the investigation" [marginal (a)]
    WHEN `reg 87(3)(b) the disclosure is made in the exercise of a function under these Regulations, or in compliance with a requirement imposed by or under these Regulations` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) the disclosure is made in the exercise of a function under these Regulations, or in compliance with a requirement imposed by or under these Regulations" [marginal (a)]
    WHEN `reg 87(3)(c) the disclosure is made in the exercise of a function, or in compliance with a requirement imposed, by or under the Terrorism Act 2000` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(c) the disclosure is made in the exercise of a function, or in compliance with a requirement imposed, by or under the Terrorism Act 2000" [marginal (a)]
    WHEN `reg 87(3)(d) the disclosure is made in the exercise of a function, or in compliance with a requirement imposed, by or under the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(d) the disclosure is made in the exercise of a function, or in compliance with a requirement imposed, by or under the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002" [marginal (a)]
    WHEN `reg 87(3)(e) the disclosure is made in the exercise of a function, or in compliance with a requirement imposed, under any Act relating to criminal conduct or benefit from criminal conduct` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(e) the disclosure is made in the exercise of a function, or in compliance with a requirement imposed, under any Act relating to criminal conduct or benefit from criminal conduct" [marginal (a)]
    WHEN `reg 87(3)(f) P is a professional legal adviser and the disclosure falls within paragraph (6)` THEN
        IF `reg 87(6) the disclosure falls within this paragraph` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND NOT (`reg 87(7) the disclosure falls within paragraph (6)` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(f) P is a professional legal adviser and the disclosure falls within paragraph (6)" [marginal (a)]
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the disclosure does not fall within paragraph (6), or paragraph (7) takes it out
    WHEN `reg 87(3) none of these cases` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (3) lists the cases in which P does not commit the offence and says nothing of any other

-- Reg 87(8): P does not commit an offence under paragraph (2)(b) if (a) or (b).
-- src:2676 | (8) P does not commit an offence under paragraph (2)(b) if—
-- src:2677 | (a) P does not know or suspect that the documents are relevant in connection with the investigation; or
-- src:2678 | (b) P does not intend to conceal any facts disclosed by the documents from any appropriate officer acting in connection with the investigation.
@ref reg 87(8) (src:2676-2678)
GIVEN `P does not know or suspect that the documents are relevant in connection with the investigation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `P does not intend to conceal any facts disclosed by the documents from any appropriate officer acting in connection with the investigation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 87(8) P commits an offence under paragraph (2)(b)` IS
    IF `P does not know or suspect that the documents are relevant in connection with the investigation` OR `P does not intend to conceal any facts disclosed by the documents from any appropriate officer acting in connection with the investigation`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "P does not commit an offence under paragraph (2)(b) if— (a) ...; or (b) ..." [marginal (a)]
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- Reg 87(2), (3) and (8) gathered by hand (ruling E1, option B): does P commit an offence under paragraph (2)?  A defence in (3) or (8) is read first.
-- src:2658 | (2) P commits an offence if—
-- src:2659 | (a) P makes a disclosure which is likely to prejudice the investigation; or
-- src:2660 | (b) P falsifies, conceals, destroys or otherwise disposes of, or causes or permits the falsification, concealment, destruction or disposal of, documents which are relevant to the investigation.
-- src:2661 | (3) P does not commit an offence under paragraph (2)(a) if—
-- src:2662 | (a) P does not know or suspect that the disclosure is likely to prejudice the investigation;
-- src:2663 | (b) the disclosure is made in the exercise of a function under these Regulations, or in compliance with a requirement imposed by or under these Regulations;
-- src:2664 | (c) the disclosure is made in the exercise of a function, or in compliance with a requirement imposed, by or under the Terrorism Act 2000 ;
-- src:2665 | (d) the disclosure is made in the exercise of a function, or in compliance with a requirement imposed, by or under the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002 ;
-- src:2666 | (e) the disclosure is made in the exercise of a function, or in compliance with a requirement imposed, under any Act relating to criminal conduct or benefit from criminal conduct; or
-- src:2667 | (f) P is a professional legal adviser and the disclosure falls within paragraph (6).
-- src:2676 | (8) P does not commit an offence under paragraph (2)(b) if—
-- src:2677 | (a) P does not know or suspect that the documents are relevant in connection with the investigation; or
-- src:2678 | (b) P does not intend to conceal any facts disclosed by the documents from any appropriate officer acting in connection with the investigation.
@ref reg 87(2), (3) and (8) (src:2658-2667) (src:2676-2678)
GIVEN `reg 87(2)(a) P commits an offence by a disclosure likely to prejudice the investigation` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `reg 87(3) P commits an offence under paragraph (2)(a)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `reg 87(2)(b) P commits an offence by falsifying, concealing or destroying documents` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `reg 87(8) P commits an offence under paragraph (2)(b)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 87(2) P commits an offence` IS
    IF `reg 87(3) P commits an offence under paragraph (2)(a)` EQUALS JUST FALSE OR `reg 87(8) P commits an offence under paragraph (2)(b)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "P does not commit an offence under paragraph (2)(a) if" or "(2)(b) if" [marginal (a)]
    ELSE IF `reg 87(2)(a) P commits an offence by a disclosure likely to prejudice the investigation` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `reg 87(2)(b) P commits an offence by falsifying, concealing or destroying documents` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE IF     `reg 87(2)(a) P commits an offence by a disclosure likely to prejudice the investigation` EQUALS NOTHING
                  OR `reg 87(2)(b) P commits an offence by falsifying, concealing or destroying documents` EQUALS NOTHING
              THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether regulation 87 applies has not been answered
              ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "P commits an offence if— (a) ...; or (b) ..." [marginal (a)]

-- Reg 87(9): the sentence limits.
-- src:2679 | (9) A person guilty of an offence under paragraph (2) is liable—
-- src:2680 | (a) on summary conviction—
-- src:2681 | (i) in England and Wales, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding three months, to a fine or to both,
-- src:2682 | (ii) in Scotland or Northern Ireland, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding three months, to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum or to both;
-- src:2683 | (b) on conviction on indictment, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding two years or to a fine, or to both.
@ref reg 87(9) (src:2679-2683)
GIVEN `how the person is convicted` IS A `reg 86(1) mode of conviction`
      `the term of imprisonment, in months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 87(9) the term of imprisonment is within the liability` IS
    CONSIDER `how the person is convicted`
    WHEN `reg 86(1) on summary conviction` THEN
        IF `the term of imprisonment, in months` <= 3
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a)(i) in England and Wales, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding three months, to a fine or to both; (ii) in Scotland or Northern Ireland, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding three months" [marginal (a)]
    WHEN `reg 86(1) on conviction on indictment` THEN
        IF `the term of imprisonment, in months` <= 24
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) on conviction on indictment, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding two years or to a fine, or to both" [marginal (a)]
@ref reg 87(9) (src:2679-2683)
GIVEN `how the person is convicted` IS A `reg 86(1) mode of conviction`
      `where the person is convicted` IS A `Part of the United Kingdom`
      `the fine, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `the statutory maximum, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 87(9) the fine is within the liability` IS
    CONSIDER `how the person is convicted`
    WHEN `reg 86(1) on summary conviction` THEN
        IF `where the person is convicted` EQUALS `England and Wales`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "(i) in England and Wales, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding three months, to a fine or to both" states no figure
        ELSE IF `the fine, in pounds` <= `the statutory maximum, in pounds`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(ii) in Scotland or Northern Ireland, ... to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum or to both" [marginal (a)]
    WHEN `reg 86(1) on conviction on indictment` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "a fine" on conviction on indictment states no figure

§§ `Regulation 88 -- Information offences`

-- Reg 88(1): P commits an offence if, in purported compliance with a requirement imposed by or under these Regulations, P provides false or misleading information in a material particular, knowing it or being reckless as to whether it is.
-- src:2695 | (1) A person (“P”) commits an offence if, in purported compliance with a requirement imposed on P by or under these Regulations, P provides information to any person which is false or misleading in a material particular, and—
-- src:2696 | (a) P knows that the information is false or misleading; or
-- src:2697 | (b) P is reckless as to whether the information is false or misleading.
@ref reg 88(1) (src:2695-2697)
GIVEN `P provides information to any person in purported compliance with a requirement imposed on P by or under these Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is false or misleading in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN
      `P knows that the information is false or misleading` IS A BOOLEAN
      `P is reckless as to whether the information is false or misleading` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 88(1) P commits an offence` IS
    IF `P provides information to any person in purported compliance with a requirement imposed on P by or under these Regulations` AND `the information is false or misleading in a material particular` AND (`P knows that the information is false or misleading` OR `P is reckless as to whether the information is false or misleading`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person (“P”) commits an offence if, in purported compliance with a requirement imposed on P by or under these Regulations, P provides information to any person which is false or misleading in a material particular, and—" [marginal (a)]

-- Reg 88(2): the sentence limits for the offence in paragraph (1).
-- src:2698 | (2) A person guilty of an offence under paragraph (1) is liable—
-- src:2699 | (a) on summary conviction—
-- src:2700 | (i) in England and Wales, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding three months, to a fine or to both,
-- src:2701 | (ii) in Scotland or Northern Ireland, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding three months, to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum or to both;
-- src:2702 | (b) on conviction on indictment, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding two years or to a fine or to both.
@ref reg 88(2) (src:2698-2702)
GIVEN `how the person is convicted` IS A `reg 86(1) mode of conviction`
      `the term of imprisonment, in months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 88(2) the term of imprisonment is within the liability` IS
    CONSIDER `how the person is convicted`
    WHEN `reg 86(1) on summary conviction` THEN
        IF `the term of imprisonment, in months` <= 3
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a)(i) in England and Wales, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding three months, to a fine or to both; (ii) in Scotland or Northern Ireland, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding three months" [marginal (a)]
    WHEN `reg 86(1) on conviction on indictment` THEN
        IF `the term of imprisonment, in months` <= 24
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) on conviction on indictment, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding two years or to a fine or to both" [marginal (a)]
@ref reg 88(2) (src:2698-2702)
GIVEN `how the person is convicted` IS A `reg 86(1) mode of conviction`
      `where the person is convicted` IS A `Part of the United Kingdom`
      `the fine, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `the statutory maximum, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 88(2) the fine is within the liability` IS
    CONSIDER `how the person is convicted`
    WHEN `reg 86(1) on summary conviction` THEN
        IF `where the person is convicted` EQUALS `England and Wales`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "(i) in England and Wales, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding three months, to a fine or to both" states no figure
        ELSE IF `the fine, in pounds` <= `the statutory maximum, in pounds`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(ii) in Scotland or Northern Ireland, ... to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum or to both" [marginal (a)]
    WHEN `reg 86(1) on conviction on indictment` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "a fine" on conviction on indictment states no figure

