-- Reg 88(4): it is a defence to a charge under paragraph (3) to prove that the person reasonably believed (a) the disclosure was lawful or (b) the information had already and lawfully been made available to the public.  "To prove": the defendant bears it, and the standard of proof is not stated in the text.
-- src:2708 | (4) It is a defence for a person charged with an offence under paragraph (3) of disclosing information to prove that they reasonably believed—
-- src:2709 | (a) that the disclosure was lawful; or
-- src:2710 | (b) that the information had already and lawfully been made available to the public.
@ref reg 88(4) (src:2708-2710)
GIVEN `the person is charged with an offence under paragraph (3) of disclosing information` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person proves that they reasonably believed that the disclosure was lawful` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person proves that they reasonably believed that the information had already and lawfully been made available to the public` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 88(4) the person has a defence` IS
    IF `the person is charged with an offence under paragraph (3) of disclosing information`
    THEN IF `the person proves that they reasonably believed that the disclosure was lawful` OR `the person proves that they reasonably believed that the information had already and lawfully been made available to the public`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "It is a defence for a person charged with an offence under paragraph (3) of disclosing information to prove that they reasonably believed—" [ruled 2026-11-05 (b) defence]: JUST FALSE says regulation 88(4) gives no defence on these facts, not that the person has no defence at all
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a person charged with an offence under paragraph (3)": a person not so charged is outside the provision (scope, ruling (c))

§§ `Regulation 89 -- Proceedings: general`

-- Reg 89(1): who may institute proceedings for an offence.  Paragraph (5) takes Scotland out.
-- src:2712 | (1) Proceedings for an offence under these Regulations may be instituted by—
-- src:2713 | (a) order of the Commissioners;
-- src:2714 | (b) a local weights and measures authority;
-- src:2715 | (c) the Department for the Economy;
-- src:2716 | (d) the Director of Public Prosecutions; or
-- src:2717 | (e) the Director of Public Prosecutions for Northern Ireland.
@ref reg 89(1) (src:2712-2717)
DECLARE `reg 89(1) body` IS ONE OF
    `reg 89(1)(a) the Commissioners, by order`
    `reg 89(1)(b) a local weights and measures authority`
    `reg 89(1)(c) the Department for the Economy`
    `reg 89(1)(d) the Director of Public Prosecutions`
    `reg 89(1)(e) the Director of Public Prosecutions for Northern Ireland`
    `reg 89(1) some other body`

@ref reg 89(1) (src:2712-2717)
GIVEN `the proceedings are for an offence under these Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      what IS A `reg 89(1) body`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 89(1) the body may institute proceedings for an offence under these Regulations` IS
    IF `the proceedings are for an offence under these Regulations`
    THEN CONSIDER what
         WHEN `reg 89(1)(a) the Commissioners, by order` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `reg 89(1)(b) a local weights and measures authority` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `reg 89(1)(c) the Department for the Economy` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `reg 89(1)(d) the Director of Public Prosecutions` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `reg 89(1)(e) the Director of Public Prosecutions for Northern Ireland` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `reg 89(1) some other body` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the items are listed and the text does not say others are barred
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph speaks of proceedings for an offence under these Regulations

-- Reg 89(5): paragraphs (1) and (3) do not extend to Scotland.
-- src:2724 | (5) Paragraphs (1) and (3) do not extend to Scotland.
@ref reg 89(5) (src:2724)
GIVEN `where the proceedings or the authority's functions are` IS A `Part of the United Kingdom`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 89(5) paragraphs (1) and (3) extend to the place` IS
    IF `where the proceedings or the authority's functions are` EQUALS Scotland
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Paragraphs (1) and (3) do not extend to Scotland" [marginal (a)]
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph says where they do not extend and nothing of where they do

-- Reg 89(1) and (5) gathered by hand (ruling E1, option B): may the body institute proceedings in the place?
-- src:2712 | (1) Proceedings for an offence under these Regulations may be instituted by—
-- src:2713 | (a) order of the Commissioners;
-- src:2714 | (b) a local weights and measures authority;
-- src:2715 | (c) the Department for the Economy;
-- src:2716 | (d) the Director of Public Prosecutions; or
-- src:2717 | (e) the Director of Public Prosecutions for Northern Ireland.
-- src:2724 | (5) Paragraphs (1) and (3) do not extend to Scotland.
@ref reg 89(1) and (5) (src:2712-2717) (src:2724)
GIVEN `where the proceedings are` IS A `Part of the United Kingdom`
      `reg 89(1) the body may institute proceedings for an offence under these Regulations` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 89(1) and (5) the body may institute proceedings` IS
    IF `where the proceedings are` EQUALS Scotland
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Paragraphs (1) and (3) do not extend to Scotland" [marginal (a)]
    ELSE `reg 89(1) the body may institute proceedings for an offence under these Regulations`

-- Reg 89(2): proceedings by order of the Commissioners are brought in the name of an officer of Revenue and Customs.
-- src:2718 | (2) Where proceedings under paragraph (1) are instituted by order of the Commissioners, the proceedings must be brought in the name of an officer of Revenue and Customs.
@ref reg 89(2) (src:2718)
GIVEN `the proceedings are instituted by order of the Commissioners` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 89(2) the duty to bring the proceedings in the name of an officer of Revenue and Customs arises` IS
    IF `the proceedings are instituted by order of the Commissioners`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where proceedings under paragraph (1) are instituted by order of the Commissioners" [ruled 2026-11-05 (b) where]
@ref reg 89(2) (src:2718)
GIVEN `the proceedings are instituted by order of the Commissioners` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings were brought in the name of an officer of Revenue and Customs` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 89(2) the proceedings were brought in the name of an officer of Revenue and Customs` IS
    IF `the proceedings are instituted by order of the Commissioners`
    THEN IF `the proceedings were brought in the name of an officer of Revenue and Customs`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the proceedings must be brought in the name of an officer of Revenue and Customs" [marginal (c)]
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where proceedings under paragraph (1) are instituted by order of the Commissioners"; the duty does not arise, so there is no answer here: ask `reg 89(2) the duty to bring the proceedings in the name of an officer of Revenue and Customs arises`

-- Reg 89(3): a local weights and measures authority must report on the exercise of its functions whenever the FCA, or the Commissioners (where it acts under arrangements made with them), require.
-- src:2719 | (3) A local weights and measures authority must, whenever the FCA or (where the authority is acting pursuant to arrangements made with the Commissioners) the Commissioners require, report in such form and with such particulars as the FCA or the Commissioners require on the exercise of its functions under these Regulations.
@ref reg 89(3) (src:2719)
