      `the Commissioners require a report` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authority is acting pursuant to arrangements made with the Commissioners` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 89(3) the duty to report arises` IS
    IF `the FCA requires a report` OR (`the Commissioners require a report` AND `the authority is acting pursuant to arrangements made with the Commissioners`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "whenever the FCA or (where the authority is acting pursuant to arrangements made with the Commissioners) the Commissioners require" [marginal (a)]
@ref reg 89(3) (src:2719)
GIVEN `the FCA requires a report` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commissioners require a report` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authority is acting pursuant to arrangements made with the Commissioners` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authority reported in such form and with such particulars as the FCA or the Commissioners require` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 89(3) the local weights and measures authority reported as required` IS
    IF `the FCA requires a report` OR (`the Commissioners require a report` AND `the authority is acting pursuant to arrangements made with the Commissioners`)
    THEN IF `the authority reported in such form and with such particulars as the FCA or the Commissioners require`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must, whenever the FCA or ... the Commissioners require, report in such form and with such particulars as the FCA or the Commissioners require" [marginal (c)]
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "whenever the FCA or (where the authority is acting pursuant to arrangements made with the Commissioners) the Commissioners require"; the duty does not arise, so there is no answer here: ask `reg 89(3) the duty to report arises`

-- Reg 89(4): the Commissioners' investigation is treated as an assigned matter under the Customs and Excise Management Act 1979.
-- src:2720 | (4) Where the Commissioners investigate, or propose to investigate, any matter with a view to determining—
