      `the purpose is to determine whether there are grounds for believing that an offence under these Regulations has been committed by any person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose is to determine whether a person should be prosecuted for such an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 89(4) the matter is treated as an assigned matter` IS
    IF `the Commissioners investigate, or propose to investigate, the matter` AND (`the purpose is to determine whether there are grounds for believing that an offence under these Regulations has been committed by any person` OR `the purpose is to determine whether a person should be prosecuted for such an offence`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the Commissioners investigate, or propose to investigate, any matter with a view to determining— (a) whether there are grounds for believing that an offence under these Regulations has been committed by any person; or (b) whether a person should be prosecuted for such an offence, that matter is to be treated as an assigned matter" [ruled 2026-11-05 (b) where]

-- Reg 89(6): in Scotland paragraph (4)(b) is read as referring to the Crown Office and Procurator Fiscal Service.
-- src:2725 | (6) In its application to the Commissioners acting in Scotland, paragraph (4)(b) is to be read as referring to the Commissioners determining whether to refer the matter to the Crown Office and Procurator Fiscal Service with a view to the Procurator Fiscal determining whether a person should be prosecuted for such an offence.
@ref reg 89(6) (src:2725)
GIVEN `the Commissioners are acting in Scotland` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 89(6) paragraph (4)(b) is read as referring to the Crown Office and Procurator Fiscal Service` IS
    IF `the Commissioners are acting in Scotland`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In its application to the Commissioners acting in Scotland"

§§ `Regulation 90 -- Proceedings: jurisdiction`

-- Reg 90(1) to (3): where proceedings may be taken.
