    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "which cannot be taken under paragraph (1)"

-- src:2729 | (3) An offence falling under these Regulations which is committed wholly or partly outside the United Kingdom may for all incidental purposes be treated as having been committed within the jurisdiction of the court where proceedings were taken.
@ref reg 90(3) (src:2729)
