    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "committed wholly or partly outside the United Kingdom"

§§ `Regulation 91 -- Proceedings: partnership or unincorporated association`

-- Reg 91(1): proceedings against a partnership are brought in the name of the partnership, against an unincorporated association in the name of the association, and not in that of its members.
-- src:2731 | (1) Proceedings for an offence alleged to have been committed by—
-- src:2732 | (a) a partnership must be brought in the name of the partnership; or
-- src:2733 | (b) an unincorporated association must be brought in the name of the association,
-- src:2734 | and not in that of its members.
@ref reg 91(1) (src:2731-2734)
GIVEN `the offence is alleged to have been committed by a partnership` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence is alleged to have been committed by an unincorporated association` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings were brought in the name of the partnership or of the association` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings were brought in the name of its members` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 91(1) the proceedings were brought in the right name` IS
    IF `the offence is alleged to have been committed by a partnership` OR `the offence is alleged to have been committed by an unincorporated association`
    THEN IF `the proceedings were brought in the name of the partnership or of the association` AND (NOT `the proceedings were brought in the name of its members`)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be brought in the name of the partnership ... and not in that of its members" [marginal (c)]
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Proceedings for an offence alleged to have been committed by a partnership ... or an unincorporated association"

-- Reg 91(2): a fine imposed on a partnership or unincorporated association is paid out of its funds.
-- src:2735 | (2) A fine imposed on—
-- src:2736 | (a) a partnership on its conviction of an offence is to be paid out of the funds of the partnership; and
-- src:2737 | (b) an unincorporated association on its conviction of an offence is to be paid out of the funds of the association.
@ref reg 91(2) (src:2735-2737)
GIVEN `a fine is imposed on a partnership or an unincorporated association on its conviction of an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the fine is paid out of the funds of the partnership or association` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 91(2) the fine is paid out of the funds of the partnership or association` IS
    IF `a fine is imposed on a partnership or an unincorporated association on its conviction of an offence`
    THEN IF `the fine is paid out of the funds of the partnership or association`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is to be paid out of the funds of the partnership ... the association" [marginal (c)]
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A fine imposed on a partnership on its conviction of an offence"

-- Reg 91(3): rules of court on the service of documents have effect as if a partnership or unincorporated association were a body corporate.
-- src:2738 | (3) Rules of court relating to the service of documents are to have effect as if a partnership or unincorporated association were a body corporate.
@ref reg 91(3) (src:2738)
