    IF `proceedings for an offence are brought against a partnership or an unincorporated association`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In proceedings for an offence brought against a partnership or an unincorporated association"

§§ `Regulation 92 -- Offence by bodies corporate, partnership or unincorporated association`

-- Reg 92(1): the officer is guilty as well as the body corporate where the offence was committed with the officer's consent or connivance or is attributable to the officer's neglect.  The officer is a core term (S-K4).
-- src:2743 | (1) If an offence under this Part committed by a body corporate is shown—
-- src:2744 | (a) to have been committed with the consent or the connivance of an officer of the body corporate; or
-- src:2745 | (b) to be attributable to any neglect on the part of an officer,
-- src:2746 | the officer (as well as the body corporate) is guilty of the offence and is liable to be proceeded against and punished accordingly.
@ref reg 92(1) (src:2743-2746)
-- SEAM S-K4 (asking)
GIVEN `an offence under this Part is committed by a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reg 3(1) the person is an officer of the entity` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it is shown that the offence was committed with the consent or the connivance of the officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is shown that the offence is attributable to any neglect on the part of the officer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 92(1) the officer is guilty of the offence` IS
    IF `an offence under this Part is committed by a body corporate` AND (`reg 3(1) the person is an officer of the entity` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`it is shown that the offence was committed with the consent or the connivance of the officer` OR `it is shown that the offence is attributable to any neglect on the part of the officer`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `an offence under this Part is committed by a body corporate` AND (NOT (`reg 3(1) the person is an officer of the entity` EQUALS JUST FALSE)) AND (`it is shown that the offence was committed with the consent or the connivance of the officer` OR `it is shown that the offence is attributable to any neglect on the part of the officer`)
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): an answer that another provision gives is not in
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If an offence under this Part committed by a body corporate is shown— (a) to have been committed with the consent or the connivance of an officer of the body corporate; or (b) to be attributable to any neglect on the part of an officer" [marginal (a)]

-- Reg 92(2): where a body corporate's affairs are managed by its members, paragraph (1) applies to a member as if the member were a director.
-- src:2747 | (2) If the affairs of a body corporate are managed by its members, paragraph (1) applies in relation to the acts and defaults of a member in connection with their functions of management as if the member was a director of the body.
@ref reg 92(2) (src:2747)
GIVEN `the affairs of the body corporate are managed by its members` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the acts and defaults are those of a member in connection with their functions of management` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 92(2) paragraph (1) applies to the member as if the member was a director` IS
    IF `the affairs of the body corporate are managed by its members` AND `the acts and defaults are those of a member in connection with their functions of management`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the affairs of a body corporate are managed by its members, paragraph (1) applies in relation to the acts and defaults of a member in connection with their functions of management as if the member was a director of the body" [marginal (a)]

-- Reg 92(3): as paragraph (1), for a partnership.
-- src:2748 | (3) If an offence under this Part committed by a partnership is shown—
-- src:2749 | (a) to have been committed with the consent or the connivance of an officer; or
-- src:2750 | (b) to be attributable to any neglect on the part of an officer,
-- src:2751 | that officer (as well as the partnership) is guilty of the offence and is liable to be proceeded against and punished accordingly.
@ref reg 92(3) (src:2748-2751)
-- SEAM S-K4 (asking)
GIVEN `an offence under this Part is committed by a partnership` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reg 3(1) the person is an officer of the entity` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it is shown that the offence was committed with the consent or the connivance of the officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is shown that the offence is attributable to any neglect on the part of the officer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 92(3) the officer is guilty of the offence committed by the partnership` IS
    IF `an offence under this Part is committed by a partnership` AND (`reg 3(1) the person is an officer of the entity` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`it is shown that the offence was committed with the consent or the connivance of the officer` OR `it is shown that the offence is attributable to any neglect on the part of the officer`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `an offence under this Part is committed by a partnership` AND (NOT (`reg 3(1) the person is an officer of the entity` EQUALS JUST FALSE)) AND (`it is shown that the offence was committed with the consent or the connivance of the officer` OR `it is shown that the offence is attributable to any neglect on the part of the officer`)
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): an answer that another provision gives is not in
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If an offence under this Part committed by a partnership is shown— (a) to have been committed with the consent or the connivance of a partner; or (b) to be attributable to any neglect on the part of a partner" [marginal (a)]

-- Reg 92(4): as paragraph (1), for an unincorporated association other than a partnership.
-- src:2752 | (4) If an offence under this Part committed by an unincorporated association (other than a partnership) is shown—
-- src:2753 | (a) to have been committed with the consent or the connivance of an officer of the association; or
-- src:2754 | (b) to be attributable to any neglect on the part of an officer,
-- src:2755 | that officer (as well as the association) is guilty of the offence and is liable to be proceeded against and punished accordingly.
@ref reg 92(4) (src:2752-2755)
-- SEAM S-K4 (asking)
GIVEN `an offence under this Part is committed by an unincorporated association (other than a partnership)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reg 3(1) the person is an officer of the entity` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it is shown that the offence was committed with the consent or the connivance of the officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is shown that the offence is attributable to any neglect on the part of the officer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 92(4) the officer is guilty of the offence committed by the unincorporated association` IS
    IF `an offence under this Part is committed by an unincorporated association (other than a partnership)` AND (`reg 3(1) the person is an officer of the entity` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`it is shown that the offence was committed with the consent or the connivance of the officer` OR `it is shown that the offence is attributable to any neglect on the part of the officer`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `an offence under this Part is committed by an unincorporated association (other than a partnership)` AND (NOT (`reg 3(1) the person is an officer of the entity` EQUALS JUST FALSE)) AND (`it is shown that the offence was committed with the consent or the connivance of the officer` OR `it is shown that the offence is attributable to any neglect on the part of the officer`)
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): an answer that another provision gives is not in
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If an offence under this Part committed by an unincorporated association (other than a partnership) is shown— (a) to have been committed with the consent or the connivance of an officer of the association; or (b) to be attributable to any neglect on the part of an officer of the association" [marginal (a)]
